  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Show that the sequence given by the rule $a_n=2n+3$ is an arithmetic sequence.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Arithmetic sequence with common difference $2$, since $a_{n+1}-a_n=2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a_{n+1}&=2(n+1)+3\\\\a_{n+1}&=2n+5\\\\a_{n+1}-a_n&=(2n+5)-(2n+3)\\\\a_{n+1}-a_n&=2\\end{align*}$$\nThe difference between consecutive terms is constant, so the sequence is arithmetic with common difference $2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
